From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 09:13:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07209/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-28: definitive
 answer -- max_tokens IS a confirmed real bottleneck (plus a self-caught
 stale-read mistake)

Self-caught mistake, recorded honestly: a mid-run read of the results
file (before the sge arm had finished) was mistakenly reported as this
run's final result, incorrectly answering "no" to the operator's "should
we increase max context" question. arc_sge_live_path_ab.py writes its
results file exactly once, at the very end -- that read returned the
PREVIOUS run's leftover state, not this run's real data. This is exactly
the pitfall the project's Reading-Results Discipline exists to prevent,
and it recurred despite being flagged multiple times earlier this same
session.

Corrected, definitive answer from the real final data: YES, max_tokens
IS a confirmed real bottleneck. The baseline arm's round-2 failure
message now reads "[HIT n_predict=2560 OUTPUT LIMIT before completing]"
-- the model was genuinely cut off at its token budget before finishing
valid code. The sge arm fails differently -- a 300s HTTP TimeoutError,
which bypasses the detection code entirely (a bare network exception) --
a separate, wall-clock bottleneck, not a token-count one. n_ctx shows no
evidence of being a bottleneck anywhere in this REQ chain.

Final answer: raise max_tokens (confirmed-justified) AND timeout in
proportion -- neither alone is the complete fix; they need to move
together.

